My 21st level tourist had hit the castle level, having vanquished Medusa
with neither blindfold nor telepathy.  Unfortunately, I also did not have
any means of levitation, jumping, water-walking, or knocking, and I don't
think I had even so much as seen a musical instrument in this game.  And I
don't polypile (I don't count making dragon scale mail).  On the other
hand, I did know a spell of polymorph, and I had an identified ring of
polymorph control...

I had wanted to save the polymorph spell until after I had killed my first
gray dragon.  I was afraid that I might use up my spell energy and run dry
right right when I got my big chance for grey dragon scale mail.  But
then, I also didn't want to go pick through every piece of armor until I
could ID some appropriate footwear, or wait for the game to generate a
trinket for some other solution.

Really hit the spoilers (y/n)?

Finally, I stripped off my armor, slipped Frost Brand into its scabbard,
and polymorphed myself into a floating eye (floating eyes carry equipment
by telekinesis).  I was too tired, that's the only excuse I can think of.
A Xorn accosted me when I was on my way around the moat, I changed back
into a tourist, and was dragged underwater by the weight of my pack.

In my pack at the time, I had (among other things) 10 uncursed blank
scrolls, three blessed potions of water, a +3 ring of protection, a ring
of invisibility, a +4 elven cloak (I aggravated monsters and needed the
stealth), blessed rustproof speed boots, +0 gauntlets of dexterity, a
rustproof blue and green shield (total AC = -16), and a blessed rustproof
-1 long sword named Frost Brand-- I would have been invincible once I got
to the wand of wishing.

Belatedly, a thought occurred to me-- don't Vampire Lords levitate?  Has
anybody ever tried walking the moat as a Vampire Lord?

